    {"claim": "Treating discrimination as an operational cost does not prevent it; it merely provides a license to harm for firms wealthy enough to pay the premium.", "targets": ["AN-11"]},
    {"claim": "Automated circuit breakers are designed to react to known failure modes, but they are entirely blind to the structural biases that emerge from complex, opaque, and adaptive architectures.", "targets": ["AN-23"]},
    {"claim": "Independent, third-party audits are essential diagnostic tools that identify the emergent behaviors an algorithm’s own loss function is incentivized to ignore.", "targets": ["AN-22"]}
